📗
  🧷 A binder: reads typed values from what a request brought, and collects
  what is wrong with them, so that a handler says so once.

    🆕🧷 r❗️ ➡️ input
    🔡 input 🔤title🔤 1 200❗️ ➡️ title
    👌🔸🍬 input 🔤done🔤❗️ ➡️ done
    ↪️ 🚩 input❗️ 🍇
      🚨 🧨 input❗️
    🍉

  A reader never raises, and one for a required value never gives an
  optional. When the value is missing or wrong it records a message under the
  field's name and gives back something that is safe to hold and wrong to
  use: an empty text, the lower bound, 👎, the first of the choices. So a
  handler must ask 🚩 input❗️ before it uses what it read. The fields come
  from the members of the JSON body until the binder is told otherwise:
  🔎 input❗️ for the query, 📌 input❗️ for the route, 📋 input❗️ for the
  fields of a form, 🍪 input❗️ for the cookies and 🏷 input❗️ for the
  headers. 🌸 input❗️ goes back to the body.
